@startuml senku-ingestion-flush
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
top to bottom direction

title Senku Ingestion and Sharded Flush Directories

actor "Concurrent callers" as Callers
component "SenkuIngestor\n\n32 active HashMap<K,V> stripes\n32 independent mutation locks\napproximate sampled count" as Ingestor
component "Atomic rotation\nunder all mutation locks\n\n1. detach the active striped batch\n2. install 32 new active maps\n3. release mutation locks" as Rotation
component "Detached batch flush outside mutation locks\nwithout copying map nodes\n\n1. traverse detached maps directly\n2. count records per persistent shard\n3. place entry references in shard ranges\n4. sort large multi-shard batches concurrently\n5. write parts and shard-start index\n6. publish manifest.properties last" as Flush

frame "Committed staging directories" {
  folder "flush/flush-00001/\n\nmanifest.properties\nshard-index.dat\npart-00000.chunk\npart-00001.chunk\n\nscarce shard-start index [m]\nS000: shard ID, start, record count\nS001: shard ID, start, record count\n..." as Flush1
  folder "flush/flush-K/\n\nmanifest.properties\nshard-index.dat\npart-00000.chunk\n\nlater generation\ndifferent record counts" as FlushK
}

Callers --> Ingestor : put\navalanche configured hash; lock one stripe\nget; optional merge; put
Ingestor --> Rotation : sampled count reaches limit
Rotation --> Ingestor : new active striped batch\naccept puts while flush runs
Rotation --> Flush : detached immutable stripe maps
Flush --> Flush1 : flush generation 1
Flush --> FlushK : later generation

note right of Rotation
At most one detached batch is being flushed.
If the new active batch also fills, put calls wait
until the current flush advances to that batch.
end note

note bottom of Flush1
The shard count and shardFor(key) are fixed.
Mutation stripes do not change persistent shard IDs.
A logical generation may span ordered parts.
Each part is a ChunkStoreFile of compressed pages.
LargeFile composes parts without changing ChunkStoreFile.
Shard starts are opaque LargeFilePosition tokens; no page ID is exposed.
High position bits select the part; low 31 bits hold
the existing local CellPosition.
Parts rotate before a page would exceed maxEntriesPerPart.
This entry limit does not guarantee a physical byte limit.
end note
@enduml
